# THIS FILE IS TRACKED BY GIT AND THE REPO IS PUBLIC. Keep the values below EMPTY.
# Put the real test-branch connection strings in `.env.test.local` (gitignored by `.env.*.local`);
# `pnpm test:db` loads this file, then `.env.test.local` on top of it.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS NOT .env.local.
# 16 test files are gated on DATABASE_URL and skip without it, so they have never run.
# The obvious fix, loading .env.local, does NOT work: that file also carries real Mailgun,
# Stripe and Cloudinary keys, and three tests assert on behaviour when NO recipient is
# configured. Loading it makes them fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the database.
# So `pnpm test:db` loads THIS file, which should contain the database URL and nothing else.
#
# USE THE DEVELOPMENT BRANCH, NEVER PRODUCTION. These tests INSERT and DELETE rows: users,
# tenants, courses, cohorts. Pointing this at production would write test fixtures into the
# live catalog.
DATABASE_URL=
# Optional. Some scripts prefer a direct (unpooled) connection for migrations.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
